# Add UI internationalisation (English / Korean)

Context: The UI was English-only, with menu, button and help text hard-coded
across Jinja templates and page scripts. This change adds a client-side i18n
layer and a Korean dictionary, so users can switch the interface language
from the navbar user menu or from Settings > UI without touching the
templates. English remains the authoring language and the default. Two
pre-existing layout issues surfaced while testing are also fixed: uneven icon
spacing on admin-only navbar dropdown items, and inner scrollbars on the
Settings > UI cards.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/js/i18n.js`
   New translator: walks text nodes and the placeholder / title / aria-label
   attributes, follows script-generated DOM through a MutationObserver, and
   wraps alert / confirm / prompt. Lookup order is exact match, `{n}` number
   template, "known prefix: dynamic detail", then the text without trailing
   punctuation. Code, editors, SVG, form values and `translate="no"` /
   `.notranslate` / `[data-i18n-skip]` regions are never translated, so user
   data stays verbatim. The language is stored in the `ob_lang` cookie.
2. `src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js`
   Korean dictionary (about 3,200 UI strings from templates, menu_config.json
   and page scripts). Product and standard names (OWL, SHACL, Lakebase, ...)
   are left in English.
3. `src/front/static/global/css/i18n.css`
   Hides non-English pages until translation is applied (1.5s reveal
   fail-safe) and styles the active language item.
4. `src/front/fastapi/dependencies.py`
   Added `resolve_ui_lang` and the `get_ui_lang` Jinja global (cookie
   `ob_lang`, default from `ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG`, fallback `en`).
5. `src/front/templates/base.html`
   `<html lang>` rendered from the cookie, i18n assets wired right after
   permissions.js, and a Language switch added to the user menu.
6. `src/front/templates/settings.html`, `src/front/static/global/css/config.css`
   Settings > UI: new Language card below Branding (per-user, applies
   immediately). UI-section cards now size to content and the section
   scrolls, instead of each card scrolling internally.
7. `src/front/static/global/css/permissions.css`
   Admin-only navbar / subnav dropdown items keep the flex row layout, so
   their icon spacing matches the other items.
8. `app.yaml.template`
   New `ONTOBRICKS_UI_LANG` env (from `APP_UI_LANG`) sets the default UI
   language for users who have not picked one.
9. `scripts/deploy.config.sh`
   Exports `APP_UI_LANG` (default `en`) so the app.yaml renderer can fill
   the new template variable.
10. `tests/units/front/test_i18n.py`
   Coverage for language resolution, translation core (via node), dictionary
   integrity and menu coverage, asset wiring order, the language switches,
   and both layout fixes.

